# Example Caddyfile — automatic HTTPS for the webhook and the Mini App
# (Telegram requires https:// for both). Caddy fetches certificates by itself.
#
#   1. Point an A/AAAA DNS record of your domain at the VPS.
#   2. Install caddy, replace the file contents of /etc/caddy/Caddyfile:
#
# duck.example.com {
#     reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8080
# }
#
#   3. systemctl reload caddy
#   4. Set WEBAPP_URL=https://duck.example.com in .env and restart the bot —
#      it registers https://duck.example.com/api/webhook with Telegram.
